   $q$Which expression is equivalent to $(3x - 4)^2$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$3x^2 - 24x + 16$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-to-square-coefficient"},{"text":"$9x^2 - 12x + 16$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"did-not-double-middle-term"},{"text":"$9x^2 + 16$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-middle-term"},{"text":"$9x^2 - 24x + 16$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$9x^2 - 24x + 16$$q$, $q$By $(a - b)^2 = a^2 - 2ab + b^2$, the result is $9x^2 - 2(3x)(4) + 16 = 9x^2 - 24x + 16$. Writing $9x^2 + 16$ squares each term and drops the middle term $-2ab$.$q$, 'draft', null)
