   $q$Which shows $x^4 - 16$ factored completely over the integers?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$(x^2 + 4)(x^2 - 4)$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"stopped-factoring-early"},{"text":"$(x^2 + 4)(x + 4)(x - 4)$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-square-root"},{"text":"$(x + 2)^2(x - 2)^2$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"factored-sum-of-squares"},{"text":"$(x^2 + 4)(x + 2)(x - 2)$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$(x^2 + 4)(x + 2)(x - 2)$$q$, $q$First $x^4 - 16 = (x^2 + 4)(x^2 - 4)$, and then $x^2 - 4 = (x + 2)(x - 2)$, while $x^2 + 4$ does not factor over the integers. The form $(x^2 + 4)(x^2 - 4)$ is equivalent but stops before the last difference of squares is factored.$q$, 'draft', null)
