   $q$Which shows $2x^3 - 5x^2 - 8x + 20$ factored completely?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$(2x - 5)(x^2 + 4)$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"sign-error-in-grouping"},{"text":"$(2x - 5)(x + 2)(x - 2)$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$(2x - 5)(x^2 - 4)$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"stopped-factoring-early"},{"text":"$(2x + 5)(x + 2)(x - 2)$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"sign-error"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$(2x - 5)(x + 2)(x - 2)$$q$, $q$Group as $x^2(2x - 5) - 4(2x - 5) = (2x - 5)(x^2 - 4)$, then factor $x^2 - 4$ to get $(2x - 5)(x + 2)(x - 2)$. Writing $x^2 + 4$ forgets that factoring $-4$ out of $-8x + 20$ leaves the minus sign in front of the 4.$q$, 'draft', null)
