   $q$The volume of a rectangular planter, in cubic feet, is $x^3 - 2x^2 - 9x + 18$. Its three dimensions are linear expressions with integer coefficients whose product is the volume. Which are the three dimensions?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$x - 2$, $x - 3$, $x - 3$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrote-perfect-square"},{"text":"$x - 2$, $x - 9$, $x + 1$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"factored-x-squared-minus-9-wrongly"},{"text":"$x + 2$, $x - 3$, $x + 3$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"sign-error-in-grouping"},{"text":"$x - 2$, $x - 3$, $x + 3$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$x - 2$, $x - 3$, $x + 3$$q$, $q$Group as $x^2(x - 2) - 9(x - 2) = (x - 2)(x^2 - 9) = (x - 2)(x - 3)(x + 3)$. Using $x + 2$ misreads the first group, since $x^3 - 2x^2 = x^2(x - 2)$.$q$, 'draft', null)
