   $q$The system $2x + y = 7$ and $5x + 3y = 18$ is written as $AX = B$ with $A = \begin{bmatrix} 2 & 1 \\ 5 & 3 \end{bmatrix}$. Using $X = A^{-1}B$, what is the solution?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$x = 32, y = 89$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"multiplied-by-matrix-instead-of-inverse"},{"text":"$x = 3, y = -1$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"sign-error"},{"text":"$x = 1, y = 3$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"swapped-x-and-y"},{"text":"$x = 3, y = 1$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$x = 3, y = 1$$q$, $q$$\det A = 6 - 5 = 1$, so $A^{-1} = \begin{bmatrix} 3 & -1 \\ -5 & 2 \end{bmatrix}$ and $A^{-1}\begin{bmatrix} 7 \\ 18 \end{bmatrix} = \begin{bmatrix} 21 - 18 \\ -35 + 36 \end{bmatrix} = \begin{bmatrix} 3 \\ 1 \end{bmatrix}$. The choice $x = 32, y = 89$ multiplies by $A$ instead of by $A^{-1}$.$q$, 'draft', null)
