-- Passage rg4-argument-evidence-p04
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('1b94b6a2-5ab6-5ad5-9f2a-09da8dacffe1', 'rg4-argument-evidence-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-argument-evidence'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Recess Before Lunch$q$, $q$At Linden Elementary, students eat lunch first and then go out to recess. Our school should switch the order. Recess should come before lunch.

When recess comes first, students eat more of their food. Many children rush through lunch so they can get outside to play. At Hilltop School, the cafeteria workers weighed the food that was thrown away. After Hilltop moved recess before lunch, students threw away about one third less food.

Recess first also helps students behave better in the cafeteria. After running and playing, children are ready to sit down and rest. The lunch helpers at Hilltop said the cafeteria became calmer and quieter.

Students also come back to class ready to learn. Teachers at Hilltop noticed that students settled down faster after lunch. They were full and calm instead of sweaty and excited.

Some people worry that students will be too hungry to play. But recess is only twenty minutes long, and most students eat a snack in the morning.

Moving recess is an easy change. It costs nothing, and it could help every student at Linden.$q$, 'draft')
