   $q$Which account is a secondhand account of the game?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Priya's blog post, because it was posted on the internet.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Neither one, because both tell who won the final game.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"same-topic-same-source"},{"text":"The newspaper story, written by a reporter about the team.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Priya's blog post, because it tells about the last shot.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-firsthand-secondhand"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The newspaper story, written by a reporter about the team.$q$, $q$The newspaper reports on the team and calls Priya "Captain Priya Nair," so it tells the event from the outside. Priya's blog is firsthand because she played in the game and uses "I" and "my."$q$, 'draft', '77c71ca8-3ec9-5da5-b547-b1e7a2f7e617')
