-- Passage rg4-character-setting-plot-p01
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('a2dd110e-d0e9-5af9-980d-0974fb7ce197', 'rg4-character-setting-plot-p01', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-character-setting-plot'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Kite With No Tail$q$, $q$Priya Raman spent all week building a kite for the Saturday kite festival at Lakeview Park. She glued red tissue paper over a frame of thin sticks. She painted a yellow sun in the middle. It was the prettiest kite she had ever made.

On Saturday, the park was full of families. A strong wind pushed the grass flat and made the flags snap. Priya held her kite up high and ran across the field. The kite rose for a moment. Then it spun in circles and crashed into the grass.

She tried again. It crashed again. Priya's cheeks turned hot. She wanted to stuff the kite in her bag and go home.

An older boy named Mateo was flying a plain brown kite nearby. It had a long tail made of knotted rags. "Your kite is spinning because it has no tail," he said. "A tail keeps a kite steady in a strong wind."

Priya looked down at her kite. She had skipped the tail because she thought it would hide her painted sun. She took a deep breath. Then she untied the ribbon from her ponytail and the scarf from her neck. She knotted them together and tied them to the bottom of the kite.

This time, the kite climbed high and stayed there. The yellow sun glowed above the field. Priya waved at Mateo, and he gave her a thumbs-up.$q$, 'draft')
